  {
   "id": "_Us-ZbjFAQAJ",
   "from": "Yves Rosseel",
   "author": "89c9fc822e34b78c",
   "date": "2020-06-01T12:45:25Z",
   "subject": "Re: Factor Score Estimated with EBM and ML methods: sd differences",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "Hello Hugo,\r<br>\r<br>With categorical + ML, the &#39;optimal&#39; values for the factor scores are \r<br>not well defined. In the source code, I added this note:\r<br>\r<br># NOTE: &#39;true&#39; ML is simply  -1*sum(log.fy)\r<br>#  - but there is no upper/lower bound for the extrema:\r<br>#    a pattern of all (in)correct drives the &#39;theta&#39; parameter\r<br>#    towards +/- Inf\r<br># - therefore, we add a vague prior, just to stabilize\r<br>#\r<br>\r<br>Usually, a fully Bayesian approach is used for this, and lavaan&#39;s vague \r<br>prior may be too vague for the moment.\r<br>\r<br>But this mostly affects the scale. Factor scores do not need to have \r<br>unit variance.\r<br>\r<br>Note that the correlation between EBM and ML factor scores is usually &gt;0.90.\r<br>\r<br>Yves.\r<br>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "JsDTchjRAQAJ",
   "from": "Hugo Harada",
   "author": "73fb61795976b321",
   "date": "2020-06-01T16:13:53Z",
   "subject": "Re: Factor Score Estimated with EBM and ML methods: sd differences",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-size:small\">Hi, Yves!<br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-size:small\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-size:small\">Thank you for the clarification!</div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-size:small\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-size:small\">Kind regards,</div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-size:small\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-size:small\">Hugo</div></div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gmail_attr\">Em seg., 1 de jun. de 2020 às 09:45, Yves Rosseel &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">yros...@gmail.com</a>&gt; escreveu:<br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\">Hello Hugo,<br>\r\n<br>\r\nWith categorical + ML, the &#39;optimal&#39; values for the factor scores are <br>\r\nnot well defined. In the source code, I added this note:<br>\r\n<br>\r\n# NOTE: &#39;true&#39; ML is simply  -1*sum(log.fy)<br>\r\n#  - but there is no upper/lower bound for the extrema:<br>\r\n#    a pattern of all (in)correct drives the &#39;theta&#39; parameter<br>\r\n#    towards +/- Inf<br>\r\n# - therefore, we add a vague prior, just to stabilize<br>\r\n#<br>\r\n<br>\r\nUsually, a fully Bayesian approach is used for this, and lavaan&#39;s vague <br>\r\nprior may be too vague for the moment.<br>\r\n<br>\r\nBut this mostly affects the scale. Factor scores do not need to have <br>\r\nunit variance.<br>\r\n<br>\r\nNote that the correlation between EBM and ML factor scores is usually &gt;0.90.<br>\r\n<br>\r\nYves.<br>\r\n<br></blockquote></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\">\r\n-- <br>\r\nYou received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;lavaan&quot; group.<br>\r\nTo unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send an email to <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">lavaan+un...@googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r\nTo view this discussion on the web visit <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/lavaan/840f5bc8-93e3-0b83-ed40-6dde33b38dfe%40gmail.com\" rel=\"noreferrer nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/lavaan/840f5bc8-93e3-0b83-ed40-6dde33b38dfe%2540gmail.com&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792421689789000&amp;usg=AOvVaw309F9QsVoYavFoA76KX_QT\">https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/lavaan/840f5bc8-93e3-0b83-ed40-6dde33b38dfe%40gmail.com</a>.<br>\r\n</blockquote></div>"
